"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71508487?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JackatDJL","id":71508487,"login":"JackatDJL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNTA4NDg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commits/9093c18b7d84558112dee2542cea4990d272aa4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-08-20T21:20:46Z","email":"71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackatDJL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-20T21:20:46Z","email":"71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackatDJL"},"message":"why dont you want to work docker????\n\nIntroduce a LoggerSystem andCollector into SoftwareBundle\nprovide structured, thread-safe for installer and config\nthreads. Replace println!/eprintln! calls in installer/config routines\nwith Logger methods (info, error) so concurrent thread output no longer\ninterleaves unpredictably. \n\nAdd SoftwareBundle::init_logger(log_level) to create and configure the\nLogCollector with a colored console output and a level filter, and\nstore the LoggerSystem for creating per-thread Logger instances.\n\nUpdate installer and configurator flows to require a Logger parameter\nfor thread execution. Spawn installer threads only if the logger system\nis initialized, and report an error if initialization is missing. On\nthread join failures, log the panic via the logger system instead of\nprinting to stderr.\n\nThese changes enable clearer, leveled logging across threads and avoid\nmixed console output from concurrent println!/eprintln! usage.","tree":{"sha":"fb032352e4a378446175c0656858c835884d51a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/git/trees/fb032352e4a378446175c0656858c835884d51a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/git/commits/9093c18b7d84558112dee2542cea4990d272aa4f","verification":{"payload":"tree fb032352e4a378446175c0656858c835884d51a7\nparent 8543183da9b3068b27c6152d8a873b8d023f996b\nauthor JackatDJL <71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com> 1755724846 +0200\ncommitter JackatDJL <71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com> 1755724846 +0200\ngitbutler-headers-version 2\ngitbutler-change-id cdba14eb-6fa9-48de-aa0b-cb47b0d128a0\n\nwhy dont you want to work docker????\n\nIntroduce a LoggerSystem andCollector into SoftwareBundle\nprovide structured, thread-safe for installer and config\nthreads. Replace println!/eprintln! calls in installer/config routines\nwith Logger methods (info, error) so concurrent thread output no longer\ninterleaves unpredictably. \n\nAdd SoftwareBundle::init_logger(log_level) to create and configure the\nLogCollector with a colored console output and a level filter, and\nstore the LoggerSystem for creating per-thread Logger instances.\n\nUpdate installer and configurator flows to require a Logger parameter\nfor thread execution. Spawn installer threads only if the logger system\nis initialized, and report an error if initialization is missing. On\nthread join failures, log the panic via the logger system instead of\nprinting to stderr.\n\nThese changes enable clearer, leveled logging across threads and avoid\nmixed console output from concurrent println!/eprintln! usage.","reaso