e":"2025-08-08T17:31:27Z","email":"71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackatDJL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-08T17:31:27Z","email":"71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackatDJL"},"message":"chore(ci): refine rust CI detection and release versioning\n\nUpdate CI workflow to accurately detect Rust-related changes by\ncomparing commits between base and head SHAs for pull requests and\npushes, listing changed files via git diff, and checking that list for\nrelevant paths. This replaces the previous simplistic check that only\ninspected the first modified file, preventing missed CI runs on\nmulti-file commits or PRs.\n\nScope the version checks and release steps to the rust/projektwoche-setup\nCargo.toml. Adjust the version-increment check to read that path, and\nextract the version into a workflow output (steps.extract-version.outputs)\ninstead of relying on env variables. Hook the release action to use the\nextracted step output for tag and release name. These changes make\nversion detection and release tag generation robust and path-specific.","tree":{"sha":"cc7cbc7309532fe76751b369acda053f1bb49909","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/git/trees/cc7cbc7309532fe76751b369acda053f1bb49909"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/git/commits/18b1473b8572c58579dcc60c15cc0953a6878656","verification":{"payload":"tree cc7cbc7309532fe76751b369acda053f1bb49909\nparent 001528b16893d372ce4c6c9ce16f2366f6eb08b5\nauthor JackatDJL <71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com> 1754674287 +0200\ncommitter JackatDJL <71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com> 1754674287 +0200\ngitbutler-headers-version 2\ngitbutler-change-id dfc67859-ddc7-4592-a292-cc6d6f0a927a\n\nchore(ci): refine rust CI detection and release versioning\n\nUpdate CI workflow to accurately detect Rust-related changes by\ncomparing commits between base and head SHAs for pull requests and\npushes, listing changed files via git diff, and checking that list for\nrelevant paths. This replaces the previous simplistic check that only\ninspected the first modified file, preventing missed CI runs on\nmulti-file commits or PRs.\n\nScope the version checks and release steps to the rust/projektwoche-setup\nCargo.toml. Adjust the version-increment check to read that path, and\nextract the version into a workflow output (steps.extract-version.outputs)\ninstead of relying on env variables. Hook the release action to use the\nextracted step output for tag and release name. These changes make\nversion detection and release tag generation robust and path-specific.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEPe7opfFXBbOntsY/zhGGnpWe2kEFAmiWNG8ACgkQzhGGnpWe\n2kF36w/9FMhEfhAnt/VtG2n5fErrBYn0QBXM+M7WTzXNXbkj0sXcHB+zCdpN0da+\nGkvR3BtJHvEFbr1nPmUh8VM6l0iWux3ah4P6Z4fB0ms8JoStH1b3EoJa1oq2cPMj\n1+RWUp9F6Kb0B+9yXrdsiJjja7/+jU1TDF1oAsT97JcaSgg3KuKzwqTNY4JBr0eK\nOLzEndvullObhMwK1VQBW+mzWywGSKynHFbK2Qbt3xefRBD+bWvEmN5gT/hbjjBl\nU9CMmKAuTT9FtVdas210m8a3j/T9pLhRUtnhCRAsFb2t4E2xYCQwGrQ/3D2GI8I1\nSi3S2aUoH7Lg9ozPLsHFMZyYbDdBuaI5FkTU62JwSzQhgWWoOK4mb2sWpiKksYjn\n7zTOe1+JHoe5EKvLqxlCUOM8YcuhILWPJXZBxzkP+vPqZWKo230MydwJ9LSP27XG\nLhPCQrbpSzh2GOY/C3lCTkNuNvmwKWqKV1lpoR3bo9tTzofW92YgcBEVYkrg5pkW\nC/AMvdUFNxhkfKjQN0WzK8o/TO7djiYhuyp2+6jN6Y+apzEHJmYAdrxxQqLRIyW3\nxPqPSNYrWsZxgErOsK6gqYyZ2jkZiS+cv4WD833YtsLDdy81Rq9ecvAYKZ2H8kVB\nZVEXv7wLzmS/xpjwnBoRoCF5CiAqynDXrPNqZ1NIZ8a0YoDbRBc=\n=noWE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-08-08T17:31:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71508487?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com