":"https://github.com/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commit/341623982ef9320e9067ad78e21a2174383f4a9e","sha":"341623982ef9320e9067ad78e21a2174383f4a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commits/341623982ef9320e9067ad78e21a2174383f4a9e"}],"sha":"3b75469ad3cd9f1439a16e0564951c198ba79854","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commits/3b75469ad3cd9f1439a16e0564951c198ba79854"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71508487?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JackatDJL","id":71508487,"login":"JackatDJL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNTA4NDg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commits/341623982ef9320e9067ad78e21a2174383f4a9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-08-08T14:32:00Z","email":"71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackatDJL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-08T14:32:00Z","email":"71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackatDJL"},"message":"fixed issues and fixed a typo\n\nUpdate GitHub Actions and keyword checker to fix runtime\nissues and ensure reliable behavior.\n\n- Rename downloaded Linux artifact to the actual filename\n  \"projektwoche-setup-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\" so the workflow\n  finds and installs the correct binary.\n- Simplify and correct conditional checks on allow-run outputs:\n  - Use proper comparisons \"needs.allow-run.outputs.RUN_CI_CD == ''true''\"\n    and \"needs.allow-run.outputs.RUN_CI_CD == ''false''\" instead of\n    erroneous duplicated equality expressions, preventing incorrect\n    branch execution for test summary and skipped-run steps.\n- Make the shell keyword check robust by avoiding piping into a while\n  loop (which runs in a subshell) and instead feed jq output into the\n  loop via process substitution. Also stop exporting the counter from\n  the subshell and update missing_keywords in the main shell, ensuring\n  the final exit status properly reflects any missing keywords.\n\nThese changes fix CI flow and make keyword detection reliable.","tree":{"sha":"fab598107c8184d4c6e137adbad0a6409acff079","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/git/trees/fab598107c8184d4c6e137adbad0a6409acff079"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/git/commits/341623982ef9320e9067ad78e21a2174383f4a9e","verification":{"payload":"tree fab598107c8184d4c6e137adbad0a6409acff079\nparent 0e847185d2a2c0e1d84ed2156fb2c9de09a9061c\nauthor JackatDJL <71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com> 1754663520 +0200\ncommitter JackatDJL <71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com> 1754663520 +0200\ngitbutler-headers-version 2\ngitbutler-change-id 55e07783-0e39-4d25-988e-983db93de326\n\nfixed issues and fixed a typo\n\nUpdate GitHub Actions and keyword checker to fix runtime\nissues and ensure reliable behavior.\n\n- Rename downloaded Linux artifact to the actual filename\n  \"projektwoche-setup-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\" so the workflow\n  finds and installs the correct binary.\n- Simplify and correct conditional checks on allow-run outputs:\n  - Use proper comparisons \"needs.allow-run.outputs.RUN_CI_CD == ''true''\"\n    and \"needs.allow-run.outputs.RUN_CI_CD == ''false''\" instead of\n    erroneous duplicated equality expressions, preventing incorrect\n    branch execution for test summary and skipped-run steps.\n- Make the shell keyword check robust by avoiding piping into a while\n  loop (which runs in a subshell) and instead feed jq output into the\n  loop via process substitution. Also stop exporting the counter from\n  the subshell and update missing_keywords in the main shell, ensuring\n  the final exit status properly reflects any missing keywords.\n\nThese changes fix CI flow and make keyword detection reliable.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEPe7opfFXBbOntsY/zhGGnpWe2kEFAmiWCmAACgkQzhGGnpWe\n2kE3LhAAkcKVQCA9JrkUo1rx9IHh36W3rZDlf3S5YXynLdSjrYMptVFGYbq1+9Gb\nwYJ9OcoKMShNcgGstrEb2HA/VGrl22j0wA3qY852oYmPu0jefaK6XaTYSWaYyOhf\nkkKhe6nTZL9ma6QWXfvAOcYiDb4k/Qah8+OFIZI5gffKy5yC4fe3KEab0y0jCoU/\nf/PC0Z+sbDIOeN1esLFLkDLweLBDZeFkDY/SXe5RNmFZtbNb6tczBR4Tti+gTaKD\njtT9galU8bPLtnxD6REU9zBl8w12d+RIBrfnRDEeX2iplwPdLysjxjayExGP65VD\nziPn/hjXwe+DPfWP3jkOAjE1XzDxo74j9zvEOyL5jvtVsva8Lr1vJbmKGnCDwLzX\n4mOYu21/vuxf2q5ghrIVNeeQfwm15RvAdHKUEaM2JjTE4je2/VG/HU4jCc7XjyQU\n1WXICcC4hHzALT+ZpeWGog8Vdxnrjpc6LINkMH/hhfRvh6R+g+1eSsK4NWD4PRbp\niaQbznJR9F0601LwUpXgBkMG4jHpbZXAdggOtQux+WYIvJtQwoJbRPXF/7//1NTX\nA2isCzQvUZNLZ5gBAbB6e8tuepfzagi9iKCMeLuhBYgSYlCRFN/Eh3PcwDcqnz3O\nXqEfJqmSDK82Ew1a7acGEGJ9DO1RVAtsVgFkGeYEDjGXo47rB5M=\n=qI9m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-08-08T14:32:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71508487?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JackatDJL","id":71508487,"login":"JackatDJL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNTA4NDg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commit/341623982ef9320e9067ad78e21a2174383f4a9e","node_id":"C_kwDOPXRq5doAKDM0MTYyMzk4MmVmOTMyMGU5MDY3YWQ3OGUyMWEyMTc0MzgzZjRhOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commit/0e847185d2a2c0e1d84ed2156fb2c9de09a9061c","sha":"0e847185d2a2c0e1d84ed2156fb2c9de09a9061c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commits/0e847185d2a2c0e1d84ed2156fb2c9de09a9061c"}],"sha":"341623982ef9320e9067ad78e21a2174383f4a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commits/341623982ef9320e9067ad78e21a2174383f4a9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71508487?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JackatDJL","id":71508487,"login":"JackatDJL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNTA4NDg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackatDJL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/commits/0e847185d2a2c0e1d84ed2156fb2c9de09a9061c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-08-08T14:15:25Z","email":"71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackatDJL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-08T14:15:25Z","email":"71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackatDJL"},"message":"ci: run Rust CI/CD conditionally on relevant\n\nAdd an allow-run job that determines whether the Rust CI/CD workflow\nshould run based on modified files or a manual workflow_dispatch. The\njob sets RUN_CI_CD and short-circuits the rest of the workflow when the\ncommit does not touch Rust sources or relevant config, reducing wasted\nCI runs and saving compute time.\n\nMake build, test and interaction/performance jobs depend on allow-run\nand guard them with if: needs.allow-run.outputs.RUN_CI_CD so they only\nexecute when CI is required.\n\nFix check_keywords.sh by exporting missing_keywords so the counter\npersists outside the while-read subshell and reports correct counts.\n\nImprove tests/run-docker-tests.sh summary to show \"none\" for empty\narrays using parameter expansion, avoiding empty parentheses in output.\n\nCorrect the artifact download name to match the produced artifact and\nprevent download failures.","tree":{"sha":"be25e14139879da1a5246037404cc632549e9a10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/git/trees/be25e14139879da1a5246037404cc632549e9a10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJL-Foundation/projektwoche/git/commits/0e847185d2a2c0e1d84ed2156fb2c9de09a9061c","verification":{"payload":"tree be25e14139879da1a5246037404cc632549e9a10\nparent 57bd60e825f7ffb184c66b3c28f30e2061147acf\nauthor JackatDJL <71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com> 1754662525 +0200\ncommitter JackatDJL <71508487+JackatDJL@users.noreply.github.com> 1754662525 +0200\ngitbutler-headers-version 2\ngitbutler-change-id 8acee66a-b788-4980-84e0-af059158e515\n\nci: run Rust CI/CD conditionally on relevant\n\nAdd an allow-run job that determines whether the Rust CI/CD workflow\nshould run based on modified files or a manual workflow_dispatch. The\njob sets RUN_CI_CD and short-circuits the rest of the workflow when the\ncommit does not touch Rust sources or relevant config, reducing wasted\nCI runs and saving compute time.\n\nMake build, test and interaction/performance jobs depend on allow-run\nand guard them with if: needs.allow-run.outputs.RUN_CI_CD so they only\nexecute when CI is required.\n\nFix check_keywords.sh by exporting missing_keywords so the counter\npersists outside the while-read subshell and reports correct counts.\n\nImprove tests/run-docker-tests.sh summary to show \"none\" for empty\narrays using parameter expansion, avoiding empty parentheses in output.\n\nCorrect the artifact download name to match the produced artifact and\nprevent download failures.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEPe7opfFXBbOntsY/zhGGnpWe2kEFAmiWBn0ACgkQzhGGnpWe\n2kHy8g//S7dIi1Pug5WQlsBheh9EhLWjBKgELxk/TrZrv3nCorEMH0S6Eu1gfiFe\nZksZsDIDZcsMd6cOZlS0RlXcTCgKZzdfmq6gonTVkV8L4W1N1jPmPIC4skd5qvSF\nLUzgn6zCDzxnOTk1AcnJfw1HlP4dy9PzqXjMMfBoKZkJziM4WS/KowTVJN1EM48+\nS7FfUGQm36t7P6XR5qTyDV7F3O0gFTZJvvZYrkNRQVC8inp4TzJWdhhYzw8/Ui4u\nev22rxY0OL/yhqr/fQ2VeTF8TVmXTPyI93Uec3ikgpmrEgCpS+JECDa8CPMERmgK\n/nMap5Kp7cPhucoy2tmU73uyulC5/LFrUOAcne7Md5BfId1TqP5hU9Qr24J9yzNu\nFR2T1zNBrtUyNZ2cWtX73va7E/O3bcBCEKHdDb98ZIgZTN5k5Odv2+Wl6UPW+gpV\nZMjZXrm25H8E/SVRDE6bMRVjEakpCs3JZbrNRxwBBnbND8II1Viq/IDZe14+yOs3\nRINywykLcyYpQuIGkwpeGkj3En5B2NxT7IeQ3WtF9oY0uxmF8+jU8lsci4GQYsor\n8Gz8UI4LGJB94/JEcZj8jzm9pT02j/L88uGsWZSu1dtkDN/+1wSAYPNnOmdk5VHq\nRI0vOY6EzZPS84oS/OEYHoTC33ICtBLDfdZ5oSxz2FuXdT+nWkU=\n=exDM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-08-08T14:15:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71508487